from common import Batch
b=Batch('JS',101)
def q(*args,**kw): b.add(*args,**kw)
q('P','Functions','Parameter reassignment','What does this object-passing example log?','2','The parameter initially contains the caller’s object reference.~Mutating that object changes count to 2.~Reassigning the parameter to a new object does not replace item.','Track mutation separately from reassignment.','Which object does item still reference?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Guide/Functions#passing_arguments','function update(value) {\n  value.count = 2;\n  value = { count: 3 };\n}\nconst item = { count: 1 };\nupdate(item);\nconsole.log(item.count);')
q('M','Strings','Literal replacement','Which call replaces every literal occurrence of "." without treating it as a regex wildcard?','text.replaceAll(".", "-")','A string search argument to replaceAll is literal. A regex dot matches arbitrary characters unless escaped, and plain replace with a string replaces only the first occurrence.','Distinguish strings and regexes.','Do you need a global regex at all?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/replaceAll',wrong=['text.replace(/./g, "-")','text.replace(".", "-")','text.replaceAll(/./g, "-")'])
q('P','Collections','Set intersection','What does this permission intersection log?','read','intersection returns entries present in both sets.~Only read belongs to both. Neither input is mutated; avoid depending on general output order without checking the size-dependent algorithm.','Find common members.','Which permission exists in both sets?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Set/intersection','const granted = new Set(["read", "write"]);\nconst requested = new Set(["read", "share"]);\nconsole.log([...granted.intersection(requested)].join(","));')
q('W','Arrays','Deduplicate by ID','Implement uniqueById(items), keeping the first record for each primitive id and preserving input order.','function uniqueById(items) {\n  const seen = new Set();\n  return items.filter(item => {\n    if (seen.has(item.id)) return false;\n    seen.add(item.id);\n    return true;\n  });\n}\n// Expected O(n) time with typical hash-backed Sets; O(n) space.','Scan in input order.~Record each first-seen ID and retain its record.~Later duplicates are discarded. Set uses SameValueZero, so NaN IDs are treated as duplicates.','Track seen IDs, not record identities.','Which duplicate should survive?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Set','// Implement uniqueById(items).\n// ids are primitives; do not mutate items.')
q('S','Modules','Circular initialization','Two ESM modules import each other’s const values and read them during top-level initialization. Why can this fail?','An imported binding can exist before it is initialized. Reading it then throws a ReferenceError. Break the initialization cycle or defer the read until initialization has completed.','Live bindings do not eliminate temporal dead zones. Cycles are not always invalid, but eager reads can make their evaluation order observable.','Separate linking from evaluation.','Is the imported binding initialized yet?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Guide/Modules#cyclic_imports')
q('P','Descriptors','Default property attributes','What does this descriptor inspection log?','false false false','defineProperty uses false defaults for omitted writable, enumerable and configurable flags.~This differs from ordinary object-literal data properties.~Explicit flags are needed for a mutable enumerable property.','Compare descriptor defaults with literals.','What happens when flags are omitted?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object/defineProperty','const item = {};\nObject.defineProperty(item, "id", { value: 7 });\nconst d = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(item, "id");\nconsole.log(d.writable, d.enumerable, d.configurable);')
q('B','Descriptors','Accessor copying','Why does this copy lose the getter, and which line preserves descriptors?','Object.assign copies the getter’s current value. Use: const copy = Object.defineProperties({}, Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptors(source));','assign reads source values and invokes the getter.~The target receives a normal data property.~Copying descriptors preserves accessors and flags; it still does not clone nested objects.','A copy can copy values or descriptors.','Which API returns accessor definitions?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object/getOwnPropertyDescriptors','const source = { get now() { return Date.now(); } };\nconst copy = Object.assign({}, source);')
q('M','Descriptors','Accessor restrictions','Which descriptor is invalid because it mixes data and accessor descriptor fields?','{ value: 1, get() { return 1; } }','A property descriptor cannot simultaneously define value/writable and get/set. Enumerable and configurable flags are allowed with either descriptor category.','Identify the two descriptor categories.','Which fields belong to competing categories?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object/defineProperty',wrong=['{ value: 1, writable: true }','{ get() { return 1; }, enumerable: true }','{ set(value) {}, configurable: true }'])
q('T','Proxy','Read interception','Trace the proxy read and give its output.','get:count\n3','Reading proxy.count enters the get trap.~The trap logs the key.~Reflect.get performs the underlying read with the supplied receiver. Reflect does not automatically bypass a different proxy passed as its target.','A property access can invoke a trap.','Which log happens before returning the value?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Proxy/Proxy/get','const proxy = new Proxy({ count: 3 }, {\n  get(target, key, receiver) {\n    console.log(`get:${String(key)}`);\n    return Reflect.get(target, key, receiver);\n  }\n});\nconsole.log(proxy.count);')
q('B','Proxy','set trap result','Why does assignment throw in strict mode although the target was changed, and how should the trap return?','The trap returns undefined, a falsy success signal. Use: return Reflect.set(target, key, value, receiver);','The trap updates target but returns no value.~Strict assignment interprets the falsy trap result as failure and throws.~Forwarding through Reflect.set returns the proper boolean and preserves receiver semantics.','Assignment needs a success signal.','What does the trap return implicitly?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Proxy/Proxy/set','"use strict";\nconst proxy = new Proxy({}, {\n  set(target, key, value, receiver) {\n    target[key] = value;\n  }\n});\nproxy.count = 1;')
q('P','Proxy','Invariant enforcement','What error name is logged when the proxy lies about a frozen value?','TypeError','count is a non-writable, non-configurable own data property.~The get trap must report its actual value.~Returning 2 violates a proxy invariant, so the engine throws.','Proxy traps have constraints.','Can a trap contradict a fixed property?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Proxy/Proxy/get#invariants','const target = Object.freeze({ count: 1 });\nconst proxy = new Proxy(target, { get() { return 2; } });\ntry {\n  console.log(proxy.count);\n} catch (error) {\n  console.log(error.name);\n}')
q('C','Proxy','Receiver forwarding','Why pass receiver to Reflect.get inside a get trap?','It preserves the this value used by an accessor. That matters when the property is inherited or accessed through a proxy. Omitting it makes the target the default receiver instead.','Reading target[key] is not always equivalent. Accessor behavior can depend on this, so forwarding the receiver preserves the intended property-access semantics.','Think about getters.','Which object becomes the getter’s this?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Reflect/get')
q('P','Proxy','Revocable access','What error name is logged after revocation?','TypeError','Proxy.revocable creates a proxy and a revoke function.~Revocation disables subsequent operations through that proxy.~The original target remains a separate usable object if another reference exists.','Revocation affects the wrapper.','Can a revoked proxy forward operations?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Proxy/revocable','const { proxy, revoke } = Proxy.revocable({ id: 1 }, {});\nrevoke();\ntry {\n  console.log(proxy.id);\n} catch (error) {\n  console.log(error.name);\n}')
q('S','Memory','WeakRef reliability','Can WeakRef be the only storage for a shopping-cart item that must remain available until checkout?','No, required application state needs a strong owner. A weakly referenced object may become unavailable after garbage collection. Use WeakRef only when disappearance is acceptable and recoverable.','Garbage collection timing is not a business lifecycle. A cache miss can be acceptable; losing the only copy of required data is not.','Ask whether disappearance is allowed.','Can the value be reconstructed?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/WeakRef')
q('M','Memory','FinalizationRegistry guarantees','Which statement is safe about a FinalizationRegistry cleanup callback?','Its execution and timing are not guaranteed.','Finalization is nondeterministic and may not run before process or page termination. Explicit cleanup is required for correctness-sensitive resources.','Collection is not a timer.','What happens if the page exits?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/FinalizationRegistry',wrong=['It runs immediately when the last variable is reassigned.','It always runs before the next timer.','It guarantees that network connections are closed on page exit.'])
q('C','Memory','WeakMap enumeration','Why does WeakMap not expose a keys iterator or size?','Keys can become unreachable independently of the map. Enumerating them would expose garbage-collection-dependent state. The API instead requires an existing key for lookup.','Keeping a separate strong-key list defeats weak-key retention benefits. Use Map when deterministic enumeration is a requirement.','Consider collection observability.','Would listing keys keep them alive?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/WeakMap#why_weakmap')
q('W','Cloning','Cycle-aware plain-object clone','Write clonePlain(value) for arrays and plain data objects containing only primitives or those containers. Support cycles; ignore symbols, accessors and custom prototypes by contract.','function clonePlain(value, seen = new WeakMap()) {\n  if (value === null || typeof value !== "object") return value;\n  if (seen.has(value)) return seen.get(value);\n  const copy = Array.isArray(value) ? new Array(value.length) : {};\n  seen.set(value, copy);\n  for (const key of Object.keys(value)) {\n    Object.defineProperty(copy, key, {\n      value: clonePlain(value[key], seen),\n      enumerable: true, writable: true, configurable: true\n    });\n  }\n  return copy;\n}\n// O(V + E) time and space for the reachable data graph.','Return primitives directly.~Register each container before visiting children to break cycles.~Reuse registered copies to preserve aliases. Defining own properties avoids __proto__ assignment semantics; recursion can overflow on very deep input.','Remember previously visited objects.','Register before recursing into children.','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/WeakMap','// Implement clonePlain(value) for the stated restricted data domain.\n// Preserve cycles, shared references and sparse array length.')
q('U','Cloning','Clone domain contracts','Follow-up to JS-117: why should that clone reject or explicitly handle Date, Map and class instances rather than silently treating them as plain objects?','Those values have semantics beyond enumerable own fields. A plain-object copy can lose internal state and prototype behavior. Restrict the input contract or use a clone mechanism that supports the required value types.','A generic-looking recursive loop is not a universal clone. Private fields and built-in internal slots cannot be reconstructed by enumerating keys.','Internal state may be invisible.','Does Object.keys describe a Map’s entries?','mdn:Web/API/Web_Workers_API/Structured_clone_algorithm')
q('P','Cloning','Transfer ownership','What byte lengths are logged after transferring this buffer?','0 4','The transfer option moves the ArrayBuffer’s backing storage to the clone.~The original buffer becomes detached with byteLength zero.~Transfer avoids retaining two usable copies of that buffer.','Transfer differs from copying.','Can the original keep using the transferred bytes?','mdn:Web/API/Window/structuredClone#transferring_values','const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(4);\nconst copy = structuredClone(buffer, { transfer: [buffer] });\nconsole.log(buffer.byteLength, copy.byteLength);')
q('P','Classes','Private-field receiver','What error name is logged when borrowing this method?','TypeError','The method accesses a private field.~The supplied plain object lacks the class’s private brand.~A public property with a similar name would not satisfy that check.','Private fields are not string keys.','Was the receiver created with this class’s private state?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Classes/Private_elements','class Counter {\n  #count = 1;\n  read() { return this.#count; }\n}\ntry {\n  console.log(Counter.prototype.read.call({}));\n} catch (error) {\n  console.log(error.name);\n}')
q('P','Classes','super method receiver','What does the inherited label log?','admin:user','Child.label calls the parent implementation with the same receiver.~The parent reads this.role from the child instance.~super selects a method; it does not replace this with the parent prototype.','Separate method lookup from receiver.','Which instance calls the parent method?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/super','class Base {\n  label() { return this.role; }\n}\nclass Child extends Base {\n  role = "admin";\n  label() { return `${super.label()}:user`; }\n}\nconsole.log(new Child().label());')
q('C','Classes','Composition tradeoff','When would you compose a storage adapter into a service instead of subclassing the service for each backend?','Compose when storage is an independent replaceable dependency. Give the adapter a small explicit contract. Reserve inheritance for a meaningful substitutable relationship with stable shared behavior.','Composition avoids binding storage variation to a class hierarchy. It still needs a clear contract; moving methods into arbitrary objects does not automatically improve design.','Identify independent axes of change.','Is the backend a dependency or a subtype?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Classes/extends#avoiding_inheritance')
q('T','Coercion','Symbol.toPrimitive hint','What does this custom conversion log?','default\n7','Addition requests primitive conversion with the default hint.~The custom method logs the hint and returns number 5.~Numeric addition then produces 7. Returning a nonprimitive would throw.','Conversion occurs before addition.','Which hint does + request?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Symbol/toPrimitive','const value = {\n  [Symbol.toPrimitive](hint) {\n    console.log(hint);\n    return 5;\n  }\n};\nconsole.log(value + 2);')
q('M','Coercion','Boolean wrapper trap','Why does if (new Boolean(false)) enter its branch?','The wrapper is an object, and objects are truthy.','The Boolean object’s wrapped primitive does not control ordinary truthiness. Boolean(false) without new returns the primitive false instead.','The runtime type matters.','Is this a primitive boolean?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Boolean',wrong=['The constructor changes false into the primitive true.','if invokes valueOf automatically for every object.','Boolean wrappers are only truthy in sloppy mode.'])
q('P','Functions','Default parameter scope','What error name is logged?','ReferenceError','Default initializers run in a parameter scope outside the function body’s scope.~The body’s local variable is not available there.~No outer value binding exists, so evaluating the default throws.','Parameters initialize before the body.','Can body declarations supply parameter defaults?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Functions/Default_parameters#description','function read(input = value) {\n  const value = 3;\n  return input;\n}\ntry {\n  read();\n} catch (error) {\n  console.log(error.name);\n}')
q('B','Functions','Callback arity mismatch','Why does this parsing callback produce unexpected NaN values, and what fixes the map call?','map passes its index as parseInt’s radix argument. Use: strings.map(value => parseInt(value, 10));','map supplies value, index and array.~parseInt interprets the second argument as radix.~The wrapper explicitly fixes radix 10, preventing accidental coupling to callback arity.','Inspect all callback arguments.','What does parseInt’s second parameter mean?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/map#using_parseint_with_map','const strings = ["10", "10", "10"];\nconst values = strings.map(parseInt);')
q('P','Iterators','Iterator closing','What is logged when the loop exits early?','1\nclosed','The first iteration receives 1 and logs it.~break closes the generator through its return method.~The finally block runs during closure. Fully consuming an iterator also completes its cleanup.','Early exit can notify the iterator.','Which block runs during generator closure?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/for...of#description','function* source() {\n  try {\n    yield 1;\n    yield 2;\n  } finally {\n    console.log("closed");\n  }\n}\nfor (const value of source()) {\n  console.log(value);\n  break;\n}')
q('P','Iterators','yield delegation','What does this delegated generator log?','1,2,3','yield* forwards values from the delegated iterable.~After that iterable completes, the outer generator yields 3.~Delegation supports iterator protocol behavior, not just array flattening.','Follow the delegated sequence.','When does the outer body resume?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/yield*','function* all() {\n  yield* [1, 2];\n  yield 3;\n}\nconsole.log([...all()].join(","));')
q('A','Memory','Bounded memoization','Design memoization for a long-lived search service with millions of possible string queries. What must the cache contract include?','Define normalization and key equality. Bound memory with a size limit or expiration policy. Specify invalidation when source data changes and decide whether failures are cached.','An unbounded Map retains every cached key and value. Memoization is correct only when a key captures all inputs that affect the result.','Caching has correctness and retention costs.','What changes invalidate a result?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Map')
q('W','Collections','Map-based LRU refresh','Implement touch(cache, key, value, maxSize) for a Map used as an LRU cache. maxSize is a positive integer; oldest keys are evicted.','function touch(cache, key, value, maxSize) {\n  cache.delete(key);\n  cache.set(key, value);\n  while (cache.size > maxSize) {\n    cache.delete(cache.keys().next().value);\n  }\n}\n// Expected O(1 + evictions) with typical Map implementations.','Delete an existing key before reinserting to refresh its order.~Map iteration exposes the oldest key first.~Evict until within the limit, including an initially oversized cache.','Map order reflects insertion.','How can an update become a new insertion?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Map','// Implement touch(cache, key, value, maxSize).\n// Mutating this cache is intentional.')
q('S','Objects','Prototype pollution defense','A dictionary must accept user-supplied string keys including "__proto__". How should its storage be designed?','Use Map or a null-prototype object with own-property checks. Validate keys if later operations have additional restrictions. Avoid blindly assigning untrusted keys into ordinary objects with prototype setters.','The special setter can make ordinary assignment differ from storing a plain key. A safe dictionary still does not make arbitrary downstream merges safe.','Choose a key-safe container.','Does the object inherit a special setter?','mdn:Web/Security/Attacks/Prototype_pollution')
q('P','Objects','Null-prototype dictionary','What do these dictionary checks log?','true false','Object.create(null) has no inherited prototype properties.~The assigned key exists as an own property.~toString is not inherited; instance methods cannot be assumed.','There is no prototype chain here.','Where would toString normally come from?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object/create','const dictionary = Object.create(null);\ndictionary.key = 1;\nconsole.log(Object.hasOwn(dictionary, "key"), "toString" in dictionary);')
q('M','Properties','Own-key ordering','For ordinary objects, which keys are listed first by Object.keys?','Array-index string keys in ascending numeric order.','Array-index keys precede other string keys, which follow insertion order. Symbols are not included. Not every numeric-looking string qualifies as an array index.','Not all keys use insertion order.','How are array indexes treated?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object/keys',wrong=['All strings in alphabetical order.','Symbols before strings.','All properties in reverse insertion order.'])
q('P','Descriptors','Reflect assignment failure','What does the nonthrowing reflection call log?','false 1','The property is non-writable.~Reflect.set returns false for this failed write.~Its value stays 1; strict direct assignment would throw instead of reporting a boolean.','Reflection can report failure.','Was the property writable?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Reflect/set','const object = Object.freeze({ count: 1 });\nconsole.log(Reflect.set(object, "count", 2), object.count);')
q('C','Functions','Bound constructor behavior','If a constructible function is bound to an object and then invoked with new, which this does its body receive?','Construction creates a new instance and uses that as this. The bound this argument is ignored for construction. Bound leading arguments still apply.','Binding a receiver does not override constructor semantics. An arrow function remains nonconstructible even after binding.','Construction has its own receiver rule.','Which parts of binding survive new?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function/bind#bound_functions_used_as_constructors')
q('P','Objects','Inherited setter','What values are logged after assigning through an inherited setter?','8 false','Assignment finds the inherited accessor setter.~The setter runs with child as this and stores _value on child.~No own value data property is created.','An inherited accessor changes assignment behavior.','What property does the setter write?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Functions/set','const base = {\n  set value(n) { this._value = n; }\n};\nconst child = Object.create(base);\nchild.value = 8;\nconsole.log(child._value, Object.hasOwn(child, "value"));')
q('W','Functions','Unary composition','Implement pipe(...functions) returning a unary function that applies the supplied synchronous unary functions left to right. Empty input is identity.','function pipe(...functions) {\n  return input => functions.reduce(\n    (value, fn) => fn(value), input\n  );\n}\n// O(k) wrapper work per call; O(k) retained functions.','Begin with the input value.~Feed each result to the next function.~With no functions, reduce returns the input. Exceptions propagate and promises are outside this synchronous contract.','Think of a rolling value.','What is the identity pipeline?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/reduce','// Implement pipe(...functions).\n// pipe(x => x + 1, x => x * 2)(3) returns 8.')
q('S','Arrays','Sort comparator lawfulness','A comparator returns a > b ? 1 : 0. Why is this unreliable for sorting distinct numbers?','It never reports that a should precede b. It violates the expected antisymmetry of comparisons. Return a negative, zero or positive value consistently, such as a - b for finite numbers.','Sorting algorithms assume a well-formed comparator. Different engines can produce different results when those assumptions are violated.','Compare both argument orders.','What should compare(1, 2) return?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/sort#sorting_with_non-well-formed_comparator')
q('P','Numbers','Safe integer boundary','What does this comparison log?','true','MAX_SAFE_INTEGER is the last integer before adjacent-integer distinctions can be lost.~The two additions round to the same representable Number.~BigInt is suitable when exact larger integers are required.','Number has finite integer precision.','Are both mathematical results representable?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Number/MAX_SAFE_INTEGER','const n = Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER;\nconsole.log(n + 1 === n + 2);')
q('B','Serialization','BigInt JSON','Why does serialization throw, and how can this payload preserve the identifier exactly?','JSON.stringify does not serialize BigInt by default. Use: JSON.stringify({ id: String(id) });','The BigInt value reaches JSON serialization without a conversion rule.~Serialization throws TypeError.~A decimal string preserves the integer exactly; converting to Number can lose precision.','JSON has fewer types than JavaScript.','Can the identifier use a string contract?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON/stringify#exceptions','const id = 9007199254740993n;\nJSON.stringify({ id });')
q('S','Strings','Unicode normalization','Two visually identical user labels have different Unicode compositions. How would you compare them under a canonical-equivalence contract?','Normalize both strings to the same canonical form, commonly NFC. Compare the normalized results. Keep locale-sensitive case or accent rules separate from normalization.','Normalization handles canonical composition differences but is not universal fuzzy matching. Compatibility forms can intentionally erase additional distinctions and need a deliberate contract.','Identical appearance can have different encoding.','Which operation canonicalizes composition?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/String/normalize')
q('M','Modules','Import namespace immutability','A consumer executes namespace.count = 3 on an ESM namespace object. Which expectation is correct?','The consumer cannot reassign the exported binding through the namespace.','Namespace properties expose live exports but are not writable by consumers. Updating belongs to the exporting module or to an explicitly exposed operation.','Live does not mean externally assignable.','Who owns the export binding?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/import#module_namespace_object',wrong=['It updates the exporter’s let binding.','It creates a private shadow property on the namespace.','It only succeeds for const exports.'])
q('A','Modules','Top-level await dependency','What architectural effect can top-level await in a configuration module have on its importers?','Dependent module evaluation waits for that asynchronous work. Independent branches may still evaluate. Keep critical initialization deliberate and avoid unnecessary serial dependencies.','Top-level await does not block the main thread like synchronous I/O. It can still delay when dependent modules become ready, which affects startup latency.','Distinguish blocking evaluation from blocking the thread.','Which modules depend on the awaited result?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/await#top_level_await')
q('P','Iterators','Single-use iterator','What does consuming the same generator twice log?','1,2\n0','The first spread advances the iterator to completion.~The second spread finds it already done and produces an empty array.~Calling the generator function again would create a fresh iterator.','An iterator stores progress.','Was a new iterator created?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Iteration_protocols','function* values() {\n  yield 1;\n  yield 2;\n}\nconst iterator = values();\nconsole.log([...iterator].join(","));\nconsole.log([...iterator].length);')
q('C','Memory','Closure retention','How can a long-lived event callback keep a large data structure alive after the creating function returns?','The callback can retain its lexical environment. Referenced data remains reachable through that callback. Remove the callback and other strong references when the owning feature is disposed.','Function return does not imply captured data becomes unreachable. Garbage collection follows reachability rather than textual scope lifetime.','Trace the retaining path.','Who still holds the callback?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Memory_management')
q('W','Rate limiting','Leading throttle','Implement a leading-only throttle(fn, wait) using performance.now. Suppressed calls are dropped; preserve this and arguments. The first call must run.','function throttle(fn, wait) {\n  let previous = -Infinity;\n  return function (...args) {\n    const now = performance.now();\n    if (now - previous >= wait) {\n      previous = now;\n      return fn.apply(this, args);\n    }\n  };\n}\n// O(1) wrapper time and retained state.','Initialize the previous time so the first call passes.~Invoke only when the elapsed interval reaches wait.~No trailing timer exists, so the final suppressed call is deliberately dropped.','Track the last admitted call.','How do you admit the very first call?','mdn:Glossary/Throttle','// Implement throttle(fn, wait).\n// wait is positive; fn is synchronous; no trailing call is required.')
q('U','Memory','WeakRef dereference ownership','Follow-up to JS-114: after dereferencing a WeakRef, why store the result in a local variable before using it repeatedly?','A local variable provides a strong reference to the returned object. Check once whether deref returned undefined. Use that stable local for the operation rather than repeatedly treating a weak lookup as required storage.','WeakRef has job-level liveness guarantees, but the ownership pattern remains clearer and supports asynchronous boundaries when the local is retained. Do not infer a garbage-collection schedule.','Promote an optional lookup into a local reference.','What does a local variable retain?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/WeakRef/deref')
q('P','Objects','Delete reveals prototype','What does this configuration lookup log after deletion?','default','Deleting an own configurable property removes the shadowing value.~Lookup then finds the prototype’s value.~Deletion does not remove the inherited property or set the value to undefined.','Lookup continues after own properties.','What is revealed by removing the shadow?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/delete','const defaults = { mode: "default" };\nconst config = Object.create(defaults);\nconfig.mode = "custom";\ndelete config.mode;\nconsole.log(config.mode);')
q('A','Immutability','Persistent state boundaries','A shared state object contains a Map. Is Object.freeze(state) sufficient to prevent consumers changing Map entries?','No, freezing the outer object does not freeze the Map’s internal entries. Even freezing the Map object does not disable its set and delete operations. Expose controlled operations or immutable snapshots according to the ownership contract.','Property descriptors govern object properties, not every built-in internal slot. A read-only API must cover the actual mutation operations of the stored data structure.','Distinguish fields from internal collection state.','Which method mutates the Map’s entries?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Object/freeze')
q('U','Proxy','Proxy identity','Follow-up to JS-109: should a cache keyed by target automatically recognize proxy as the same key?','No, a proxy and its target have different object identities. Map and WeakMap do not automatically unwrap proxy keys. Choose a consistent key identity at the API boundary.','Transparent operation forwarding does not imply identity equality. Mixing targets and proxies can create duplicate cache entries even when their visible properties match.','Forwarding and identity are separate.','Does wrapping create a new object?','mdn:Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Proxy')
b.save('batch03')
